|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></td>\t\t\t<td>(iii) <math><mrow><mrow><munder><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">lim</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>&#8734;</mi></mrow></munder></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&#8242;</mi></mrow></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>&#8734;</mi></math></td>\t\t\t<td>(R) <math><msup><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&#8242;</mi></mrow></msup></math> is increasing in (0, 1)</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(IV) <math><msup><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&#8242;</mi><mi>&#8242;</mi></mrow></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> for some <math><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>e</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></td>\t\t\t<td>(iv) <math><mrow><mrow><munder><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">lim</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>&#8734;</mi></mrow></munder></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&#8242;</mi><mi>&#8242;</mi></mrow></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td>(S) <math><msup><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&#8242;</mi></mrow></msup></math> is decreasing in <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><msup><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table>Which of the following options is the only Correct combination?"
